The below is attributable to Principal Deputy Spokesperson Tommy Pigott:

Secretary of State Marco Rubio spoke today with Ecuadorian President Daniel Noboa about ongoing regional efforts to promote stability in Venezuela and the recent law enforcement operation in Venezuela on January 3. Secretary Rubio thanked President Noboa for Ecuador’s partnership in confronting narcoterrorism and strengthening security throughout our hemisphere. Secretary Rubio noted the United States’ commitment to continue close coordination to advance regional security.